From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Frank Chang <frank.aka.hao.hao@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 13:28:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] arm64: dts: rockchip: tinker-edge-r: add the cpuinfo
 node for the SoC serial

/proc/cpuinfo showed "Serial: 0000000000000000" and /proc/device-tree has
no serial-number under extlinux boot (ASUS's U-Boot only adds it on the
Android boot path), so nothing on the board had a stable per-board ID.
rk3399.dtsi defines the eFuse cpu-id cell but no rockchip,cpuinfo node;
with one, the driver mixes the 16-byte CPU ID the way Rockchip's U-Boot
derives serial#, which reproduces the board's stock serial number
(96bb2a439d8ef209 on the board checked).
---
 .../boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399pro-tinker-edge-r.dtsi    | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399pro-tinker-edge-r.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399pro-tinker-edge-r.dtsi
index 73aab9014..1e56a6473 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399pro-tinker-edge-r.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399pro-tinker-edge-r.dtsi
@@ -192,6 +192,17 @@ simple-audio-card,codec {
 		};
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * The SoC serial number (/proc/cpuinfo "Serial") from the eFuse CPU ID,
+	 * mixed the way Rockchip's U-Boot derives serial# - the board's stock
+	 * serial number.  rk3399.dtsi has the cell but no cpuinfo node.
+	 */
+	cpuinfo {
+		compatible = "rockchip,cpuinfo";
+		nvmem-cells = <&cpu_id>;
+		nvmem-cell-names = "id";
+	};
+
 	rk_headset {
 		compatible = "rockchip_headset";
 		headset_gpio = <&gpio0 RK_PB5 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
